       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a monitored setting is 3,200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWas this a typo or a mix-up with the daily total? Some possible intended orders:\n\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for things like acute pain or inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day).\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I can then add that to the order note, though I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
